{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Moses took the bones of Joseph.</b> While Israel was busy with the needs of the body and occupied with asking for silver and gold, Moses was occupied with the needs of the soul, in the matter of a commandment, as it is written (Proverbs 10:8): ״חכם לב יקח מצות״. And Joseph had the merit of burying his father, and therefore he merited something greater than it — this is Moses; and Moses too merited something greater than it — this is the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said (Deuteronomy 34:6): ״ויקבור אותו בגי״, and I have already written this in the matter of Joseph. And further we find that Moses needed to fulfill this commandment, for the reason that our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: in the merit of Joseph the sea split — it is written here (Genesis 39:12–13): ״וינס ויצא החוצה״, and it is written there (Psalms 114:3): ״הים ראה וינוס״ — what did it see? It saw his bones, the bones of Joseph. Of Joseph it is written (Genesis 50:21): ״וינחם אותם וידבר על לבם״, and of the sea it is written (Exodus 15): ״בלב ים״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:41.453035390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}